Troubleshooting Tips
Elasticsearch won't start:

Check Java installation: java -version
Review logs: sudo journalctl -u elasticsearch -n 50
Verify memory: free -h (needs at least 2GB available)
Filebeat not sending logs:

Check configuration syntax: sudo filebeat test config
Verify Logstash connectivity: sudo filebeat test output
Review Filebeat logs: sudo tail -f /var/log/filebeat/filebeat
No logs in Elasticsearch:

Confirm Logstash is receiving data: sudo tail -f /var/log/logstash/logstash-plain.log
Check Filebeat registry: sudo cat /var/lib/filebeat/registry/filebeat/log.json
Verify file permissions on log files: ls -la /var/log/syslog
Performance issues:

Reduce Logstash workers: Edit /etc/logstash/logstash.yml, set pipeline.workers: 2
Limit Filebeat scan frequency: Add scan_frequency: 30s to filebeat.yml inputs
Restart services after configuration changes
